---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Falck | Local Studio"
  description="Local Studio is a local-first, bring-your-own-LLM way to build with Falck, open source and in your control."
  theme="light"
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden pt-24 pb-20">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 backdrop-grid opacity-60"></div>
      <div class="absolute -top-20 left-[10%] h-[340px] w-[340px] rounded-full bg-emerald-300/40 blur-[140px] glow-pulse"></div>
      <div class="absolute bottom-[-25%] right-[8%] h-[420px] w-[420px] rounded-full bg-sky-300/40 blur-[160px] float-soft"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-6 reveal">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-white/70 px-4 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-600 border border-white/80">
          Local Studio
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-slate-950">
          A lovable, local studio for bold ideas. Bring your own model and keep your data yours.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600">
          Local Studio is Falck's "build it now" mode. It runs on your machine, works with your favorite model, and stays
          open source. Perfect for prototypes, experiments, and those "what if we just shipped it" moments.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
          <Button href="/download">Download Falck</Button>
          <Button href="/features" variant="secondary">Back to the story</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] items-center">
      <div class="space-y-4 reveal">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-emerald-500">Local by design</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-950">No cloud lock-in, no mystery bills.</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600">
          Your files stay on your machine. Your model runs locally. The studio is open source and flexible, so you can
          build without handing your idea to the cloud.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Bring your own model (or switch whenever)
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Open source, so you can see how it works
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Runs locally, even on airplane Wi-Fi that is basically vibes
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="app-window reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="app-window-bar">
          <span>Falck Desktop</span>
          <span>Local Studio</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-400">
            <span>Session</span>
            <span class="text-emerald-500">Running</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid gap-3">
            <div class="surface-muted px-4 py-3 text-sm">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <span class="font-semibold">Model</span>
                <span class="text-slate-600">Local LLM</span>
              </div>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">You are the cloud now</p>
            </div>
            <div class="surface-muted px-4 py-3 text-sm">
              <p class="font-semibold">Workspace</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">Prototype: launch-day</p>
            </div>
            <div class="surface-dark px-4 py-3 text-sm">
              <p class="font-semibold">Build</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-emerald-100/70">Live preview open</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100/80 bg-emerald-50 px-4 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-700">
            Local-first energy: "Your idea stays in your laptop".
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="surface p-6 reveal">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-emerald-500">Prototype fast</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Skip the mockup phase</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
          Build the real thing and see it immediately. No more three tools, two meetings, and a "quick deck".
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface p-6 reveal-delay-1">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-slate-500">Open source</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Inspect the magic</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
          Falck is open source, which means you can audit, tweak, and brag about it in your team channel.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="surface p-6 reveal-delay-2">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] text-slate-500">Ship smarter</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Build, then grow up</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
          Start as a prototype, then move into Team Mode when the idea sticks. No drama, same tool.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mx-auto px-6 pb-28">
    <div class="surface p-10 md:p-12 text-center reveal">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-400">Next up</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-slate-950">Move from prototype to team-ready</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        When the idea is real, let the engineers wire the guardrails and keep building in Team Mode.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <Button href="/features/team-mode">Explore Team Mode</Button>
        <Button href="/features/review-ready" variant="secondary">See the handoff</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
